{"id":"torrey:galilee","source":"torrey","name":"Galilee","slug":"galilee","seeAlso":[],"entries":[{"text":"Separated from Judea by Samaria — Joh 4:3,4.","refs":[["John",4,3,4,3],["John",4,4,4,4]]},{"text":"Upper part of, called Galilee of the Gentiles — Isa 9:1; Mt 4:15.","refs":[["Isa",9,1,9,1],["Matt",4,15,4,15]]},{"text":"Lake of Gennesaret, called the sea of — Mt 15:29; Lu 5:1.","refs":[["Matt",15,29,15,29],["Luke",5,1,5,1]]},{"text":"Kadesh the city of refuge for — Jos 21:32.","refs":[["Josh",21,32,21,32]]},{"text":"Called Galilaeans. — Ac 2:7.","refs":[["Acts",2,7,2,7]]},{"text":"Used a peculiar dialect. — Mt 26:73; Mr 14:70.","refs":[["Matt",26,73,26,73],["Mark",14,70,14,70]]},{"text":"Despised by the Jews. — Joh 7:41,52.","refs":[["John",7,41,7,41],["John",7,52,7,52]]},{"text":"Opposed the Roman taxation. — Ac 5:37.","refs":[["Acts",5,37,5,37]]},{"text":"Cruelly treated by Pilate. — Lu 13:1.","refs":[["Luke",13,1,13,1]]},{"text":"Twenty cities of, given to Hiram — 1Ki 9:11.","refs":[["1Kgs",9,11,9,11]]},{"text":"Conquered by the Syrians — 1Ki 15:20.","refs":[["1Kgs",15,20,15,20]]},{"text":"Conquered by the Assyrians — 2Ki 15:29.","refs":[["2Kgs",15,29,15,29]]},{"text":"Jurisdiction of, granted to Herod by the Romans — Lu 3:1; 23:6,7.","refs":[["Luke",3,1,3,1],["Luke",23,6,23,6],["Luke",23,7,23,7]]},{"text":"Supplied Tyre, &c with provisions — Ac 12:20.","refs":[["Acts",12,20,12,20]]},{"text":"Brought up in. — Mt 2:22; Lu 2:39,51.","refs":[["Matt",2,22,2,22],["Luke",2,39,2,39],["Luke",2,51,2,51]]},{"text":"Despised as of. — Mt 26:69; Joh 7:52.","refs":[["Matt",26,69,26,69],["John",7,52,7,52]]},{"text":"Chose his Apostles from. — Mt 4:18,21; Joh 1:43,44; Ac 1:11.","refs":[["Matt",4,18,4,18],["Matt",4,21,4,21],["John",1,43,1,43],["John",1,44,1,44],["Acts",1,11,1,11]]},{"text":"Preaching in, predicted. — Isa 9:1,2; Mt 4:14,15.","refs":[["Isa",9,1,9,1],["Isa",9,2,9,2],["Matt",4,14,4,14],["Matt",4,15,4,15]]},{"text":"Preached throughout. — Mr 1:39; Lu 4:44.","refs":[["Mark",1,39,1,39],["Luke",4,44,4,44]]},{"text":"Commenced, and wrought many miracles in. — Mt 4:23,24; 15:29-31.","refs":[["Matt",4,23,4,23],["Matt",4,24,4,24],["Matt",15,29,15,31]]},{"text":"Kindly received in. — Joh 4:45.","refs":[["John",4,45,4,45]]},{"text":"Followed by the people of. — Mt 4:25.","refs":[["Matt",4,25,4,25]]},{"text":"Ministered to by women of. — Mt 27:55; Mr 15:41; Lu 8:3.","refs":[["Matt",27,55,27,55],["Mark",15,41,15,41],["Luke",8,3,8,3]]},{"text":"Sought refuge in. — Joh 4:1,3.","refs":[["John",4,1,4,1],["John",4,3,4,3]]},{"text":"Appeared in, to his disciples after his resurrection. — Mt 26:32; 28:7.","refs":[["Matt",26,32,26,32],["Matt",28,7,28,7]]},{"text":"Accho or Ptolemais. — Jdj 1:31.","refs":[["Judg",1,31,1,31]]},{"text":"Tiberias. — Joh 6:23.","refs":[["John",6,23,6,23]]},{"text":"Nazareth. — Mt 2:22,23; Lu 1:26.","refs":[["Matt",2,22,2,22],["Matt",2,23,2,23],["Luke",1,26,1,26]]},{"text":"Cana. — Joh 2:1; 21:2.","refs":[["John",2,1,2,1],["John",21,2,21,2]]},{"text":"Capernaum. — Mt 4:13.","refs":[["Matt",4,13,4,13]]},{"text":"Chorazin. — Mt 11:21.","refs":[["Matt",11,21,11,21]]},{"text":"Bethsaida. — Mr 6:45; Joh 1:44.","refs":[["Mark",6,45,6,45],["John",1,44,1,44]]},{"text":"Nain. — Lu 7:11.","refs":[["Luke",7,11,7,11]]},{"text":"Caesarea. — Ac 9:30; 10:24.","refs":[["Acts",9,30,9,30],["Acts",10,24,10,24]]},{"text":"Caesarea Philippi. — Mt 16:13; Mr 8:27.","refs":[["Matt",16,13,16,13],["Mark",8,27,8,27]]},{"text":"Christian churches established in — Ac 9:31.","refs":[["Acts",9,31,9,31]]}],"refCount":66}
